            "review_title": "Review at Pho Dinh Restaurant 5",
            "review_text": "Kijtanat P\nBangkok, Thailand176 contributions\n0\nSolid BBQ restaurant in Saigon\nJan 2017 • Family\nI have had several chances to dine in this restaurant. There are quite a few branches within HCMC. I tried both in District 1 and 7 but I saw one in District 2 also.\n\nI suppose the quality of the meat and the taste for each of the branches are quite consistent. This restaurant specializes in BBQ although there are other menus and dishes such as hot pot. \n\nObviously, the tenderness of the meat depends on the cut and if it is imported or not. There are set lunch menus on offer, which cost between 80k-120k (most items), which are not the cheapest when compare to local street foods. But in some ways, they do represent good value as the set menu comprises of selection of desserts and fruits with tea and coffee. \n\nI would recommend ordering a la cart menu for BBQ as this is what this restaurant specializes in.\n\nPrice per person would average around 200k-250k per person.\n\nStaff are friendly but might not be able to speak English well. There is also FREE wifi throughout.\nRead more\nWritten January 3, 2017",
